  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A tall, extremely dense pastel drawing of an isometric city of synthesizer modules, cables, keyboards and tiny creatures, signed 2021.",
    "description": "A portrait format digital drawing with white border, title MODULAR at bottom left and signature with 2021 at bottom right. The whole sheet is covered in an isometric tangle of blocks, towers and panels drawn as synthesizer modules: rows of knobs, patch cables looping between units, speaker cones, faders, and at the bottom edge several piano keyboards seen in perspective. Between the modules are tiny houses, a black cat at upper left, a white dove shape at centre, bird like and horned creatures, flames, leaves and clouds. The palette is pale mint, lavender, pink and yellow with almost no dark fills apart from the thin black outlines and the cat, so the picture reads as light and even from a distance and only resolves into objects up close. The outlines are thinner than in the square Colorlands pieces.",
    "impression": "A modular synthesizer turned into a city, or a city that is secretly a patch. Signal seems to flow along the cables between neighbourhoods. The near white palette makes it feel like a blueprint or a sketch of something that is still being wired up. It rewards slow looking, and it is the most diagram like piece in the series.",
